 ## Overview
-VoxelTTO training configures the optimization of a voxel-aligned feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) module initialized from a frozen Visual Foundation Model (VFM). It solves the problem of adapting large pre-trained vision models to specific 3D reconstruction tasks via test-time optimization, keeping the VFM parameters frozen while optimizing only the lightweight 3DGS module [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard neural field training by employing a hybrid loss combining rendered depth/RGB with VFM-predicted depth alignment [S1, unofficial].
